        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:48:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66424,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 13,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Papillary adenoma of the lung is a peripheral solitary neoplasm with no lobar predilection {7357529; 23328145; 10782889}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:48:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66425,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 13,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "<p>There is typically an incidental radiological finding of a well-defined nodule.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-18T17:47:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66426,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 13,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are rare (&lt;&nbsp;30&nbsp;reported) with a male predominance and an age range of 2&nbsp;months to 70&nbsp;years (median: 34&nbsp;years) {7357529; 23328145}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:48:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66427,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 13,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "<p>Unknown</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-18T16:11:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66428,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 13,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "<p >Ultrastructural findings suggest derivation from a combination of type&nbsp;II pneumocytes and club cells, suggesting possible derivation from stem cells with bidirectional differentiation {7139574; 10782889; 23328145; 1557989}. One case has been reported with FGFR2-IIIb overexpression {22924850}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-18T16:11:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66429,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 13,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "<p>There are well-circumscribed, unencapsulated nodules/masses (reported sizes: 2&ndash;60 mm) with white-tan or yellow cut surfaces lacking gross papillae or necrosis {23328145; 1543163}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-02T10:38:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66430,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 13,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "<p>Papillary adenomas are circumscribed nodules composed of papillary structures with fibrovascular cores lined by a single layer of cuboidal epithelium without nuclear atypia or mitoses and with a low Ki-67 proliferation index {7357529; 1543163; 20941571; 3006525; 19670704}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Surface epithelial cells, but not stromal cells, are positive for TTF1, CK7, pancytokeratin, surfactant protein, and EMA {23328145; 1543163; 3006525; 14511264; 8290804}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Sclerosing pneumocytoma is composed of two cell types, with papillary structures containing a TTF1-positive cellular rather than a fibrovascular core and more-varied growth patterns, including papillary, sclerotic, haemorrhagic, and solid growth {23328145; 12405908}.</p>\r\n<p>Alveolar adenomas are usually encapsulated and comprise multiple cysts lined by type&nbsp;II pneumocytes with characteristic spindle/inflammatory stroma and without papillary morphology {10029443; 18184418}.</p>\r\n<p>Papillary adenocarcinomas generally show a greater degree of cellular proliferation, nuclear atypia, complex branching architecture, and infiltrative growth. Mitotic activity and necrosis may be present.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-18T16:12:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66431,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 13,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cytological features include cohesive papillary clusters with bland-appearing medium-sized epithelial cells with no nuclear atypia, prominent nucleoli, or pleomorphism {27040894}. Papillary adenoma can be difficult to distinguish from papillary adenocarcinoma cytologically {15893002}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:48:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66432,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 13,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Diagnostic molecular pathology is not clinically required {23328145; 24727320}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:48:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66433,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 13,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Unencapsulated circumscribed peripheral papillary glandular neoplasm with a single layer of cytologically bland cuboidal to columnar cells lining fibrovascular cores</li>\r\n<li>No nuclear atypia, minimal to no mitoses, no necrosis, no complex branching architecture, and absence of invasion</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Expression of TTF1</li>\r\n</ul>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-18T16:12:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66434,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 13,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:48:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66435,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 13,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Behaviour is benign and resection is curative {23328145; 3006525; 10782889; 16204011; 29017679; 26474555}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:48:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
